{"id": "EUVD-2026-86760", "enisaUuid": "9577982b-6424-3761-937d-6d254113ae10", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbootconfig: Fix integer overflow in initrd size check\n\nSashiko reported that in get_boot_config_from_initrd(), a crafted initrd\nwith a huge bootconfig size (such as 0xFFFFFFFF) can cause the pointer\narithmetic:\n\n    data = ((void *)hdr) - size;\n\nto wrap around on 32-bit systems (or when pointer subtraction overflows).\nBecause data wraps around, the subsequent bounds check:\n\n    if ((unsigned long)data < initrd_start)\n\nevaluates to false, bypassing the check. The kernel then calls\nxbc_calc_checksum(data, size), which attempts to read 4GB of memory,\nhitting unmapped pages and triggering a fatal kernel page fault during\nearly boot. Furthermore, on 64-bit systems with an initrd > 4.29 GB, an\nunbounded 32-bit size can similarly bypass the initrd_start check.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Ensuring the initrd is at least large enough to contain the bootconfig\n   footer and verifying hdr is within the initrd bounds.\n2. Checking that size does not exceed XBC_DATA_MAX and does not exceed\n   the available space between initrd_start and hdr before performing\n   pointer subtraction.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97be05f33f79342ea65d9b99c9ad07a93b8eef5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d45bc0f8cdf606d5409b5f64a8a6609f6520c03", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d4343a411eaa182d323ab5b149496416015f27d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bff9a1579e2c9b2a59fdf3793becc9d7bf5ff1a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7812d6dab0698001e50e8c2f901e17da3eb6f429"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97906", "GHSA-rh89-37w4-pmjq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "28070de3-5f46-3c25-a0b0-8300909705be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "3fd8a250-26f5-3833-8f89-1c1e182dd8a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3fdc4d00-3180-362f-97c2-e751c91cac22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de462e5f10718517bacf2f84c8aa2804567ef7df <4d45bc0f8cdf606d5409b5f64a8a6609f6520c03"}, {"id": "46d0c589-f141-3385-8ed8-8bbc9a002e7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de462e5f10718517bacf2f84c8aa2804567ef7df <97be05f33f79342ea65d9b99c9ad07a93b8eef5a"}, {"id": "5f2feb1f-4c53-3498-91b2-da3d084684fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "765c85b4-40f2-32e5-a678-8bd9d719832f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "899c551b-ca40-3683-a66c-8649d839b78b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a0454907-ebac-33e0-bf14-c002361c1a03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de462e5f10718517bacf2f84c8aa2804567ef7df <7812d6dab0698001e50e8c2f901e17da3eb6f429"}, {"id": "c0d8458e-1ba3-33ff-96f9-1a2cb9cd1107", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "df26edc2-f550-3ffc-9a13-43b1fb824085", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e5766da0-6ce7-3fbb-9148-5d65a2a2689a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de462e5f10718517bacf2f84c8aa2804567ef7df <bff9a1579e2c9b2a59fdf3793becc9d7bf5ff1a6"}, {"id": "eea767d5-1c26-3372-9230-b4ac4d65efe1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de462e5f10718517bacf2f84c8aa2804567ef7df <8d4343a411eaa182d323ab5b149496416015f27d"}, {"id": "fef45dc2-ae50-3ff6-b9c7-aeed58967259", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32394df25d8e46935b442b429d74b37885c4f092"}, {"id": "ff725bd2-d605-318a-8ab4-757c17ae9f63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6.14 <5.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "18d0ee86-124d-3755-bff6-4e86d29a2a0c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}